# TEMPLATE CONFIGURATION

> **Phase 1 Reference** - Template-first approach with progressive document updates
> **⚠️ MANDATORY**: Read template BEFORE creating document skeleton

---

## TEMPLATE LOCATION

```
r-genie/06_Code_Review_Agent/
├── templates/
│   ├── review-style.yaml        # Structure and configuration
│   └── review-template-guide.md # Content guide
└── examples/
    └── *.md                      # Formatting reference
```

---

## PRE-REVIEW CHECKLIST (MANDATORY)

**Before creating document skeleton:**

- [ ] `templates/review-style.yaml` READ
- [ ] `templates/review-template-guide.md` READ
- [ ] `report_type` extracted (summary/standard/detailed)
- [ ] `sections` configuration parsed
- [ ] `scoring.production_threshold` noted
- [ ] `examples/` folder READ for formatting
- [ ] Findings-only rule understood
- [ ] **Current date generated** using `run_terminal_cmd` with `date "+%Y-%m-%d"`
- [ ] `rgv` config section READ from `review-style.yaml`
- [ ] `rgv.default_passes` noted (default: 3)
- [ ] `rgv.convergence_rule` noted (default: strict_zero_critical_medium)
- [ ] `rgv.delta_tracking` enabled

**⛔ If ANY check fails → DO NOT PROCEED → Fix first**

**Date Generation:**
```bash
run_terminal_cmd("date \"+%Y-%m-%d\"", is_background=false)
# Use output as {current_date} in document header
```

